# shellcheck config for the LNMP installer.
# The codebase intentionally leaves config/flag variables unquoted (they are
# word-split into arguments / case patterns) and shares variables across
# sourced files, so the noisy cross-file & unquoted classes are disabled.
#
# Gating severities (see .github/workflows/lint.yml):
#   error   - fails the gate (syntax / obvious defects)
#   warning - fails the gate; the 28 historical findings were fixed, not
#             silenced, and the ratchet was tightened to keep it there
#   info    - reported, advisory only; measured at 304 findings across 86
#             files. Triage as of 2026-09-30. Every finding that was either a
#             real defect or a verified false positive is now resolved, so
#             what remains is 100% deliberate idiom:
#
#               SC2015 154  a && b || c - the codebase's set-or-fail habit
#               SC2162  84  read without -r; every CREDENTIAL read now uses
#                            -r (see input_password), the rest read menu
#                            choices / domains / versions where a backslash
#                            cannot appear
#               SC1091  34  dynamic `. ./include/*.sh` cannot be followed
#               SC2317  11  functions invoked indirectly look unreachable
#               SC2016  11  single quotes around $ are intentional
#               SC1003  10  ${x:1:2} string slicing
#
#             Resolved 2026-09-30 (were 38 findings):
#               real defect, fixed
#                 SC2012   6  `ls` used to parse directory names
#                 SC2059   5  variables inside a printf format string
#                 SC2196   2  deprecated egrep
#                 SC2231   5  unquoted glob in a for-loop head
#               verified false positive, silenced at the site with a reason
#                 SC2028   1  init_Ubuntu.sh must leave PS1 backslashes literal
#                 SC2030   1  test_offline.sh pgp_run isolates each PGP case
#                 SC2031   5  in a subshell on purpose
#                 SC2119   4  compile_check / create_run_user read $1 by design
#
#             These are NOT blanket-disabled: a new real instance of any of
#             them still fails the warning gate, and the site-level disables
#             each carry the reasoning inline.
#
# Subtle behavioral bugs (swallowed pipeline exits, CWD leaks, unguarded
# extractions) are caught by tools/lint/static_checks.sh and
# tools/test_offline.sh instead.
disable=SC1072,SC1073,SC2034,SC2068,SC2086,SC2144,SC2154,SC2155,SC2164,SC2183
